[{:seon.task/name "no-clipping-functions"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-21: \"no clipping functions, only general improvements to the one render function and custom render functions for both html and ai when we know that output needs to be improved for context.\" Session RENDER; answers seon.fences/no-clip-in-renders (audit FENCES #47-49, its two proofs included here). Found: seon.render.ui/clip and /line (fixed character cuts with a bare …, used 24 times in seon.render.ui and 4 in seon.render.ai); bare top-N lists with no count of what they left (ui tile-tasks take 40 rows and take 8 attempts, tile-fx take 6 spent, tile-errors take-last 6, test-dots take 24, agent-card take-last 6 evals, ai section-work take 8 / take 5, section-costly take 5, section-events take 8, problems take-last 3 errors); seon.agent-proc's running form cut at 200 characters (agent_proc.clj:72,75) before it reaches root; seon.context/near's 30-character window. Replace each with: `seon.print/prose`, the one printer's face for text a person or a model reads as prose (a string shown unquoted under a token budget; a cut keeps whole lines and words where it can and says what it omitted, +N lines, +N chars, and how to read the rest when it has a source); every bounded list says how many more and where they are; the agent's running form travels whole. Delete clip and line. Also found and fixed: the stylesheet's own clips (text-overflow: ellipsis on forms, stream rows, the running form and branch; -webkit-line-clamp on the task; max-height with overflow hidden on printed values; a card hiding five of its six evaluations under a \"+N more\" that counted one), each replaced by the render's budget; the server's seon_context answered the block as an escaped string literal under the reply budget (server.clj :context, mcp.clj), now the text; the agent page's context was printed at 2,000 tokens while the model reads 16,000; root's context sized tokens at 4 chars while the printer sizes 3.2."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.print-test/prose-says-what-it-omitted
                      seon.render-test/no-cut-on-the-page-drops-silently
                      seon.render-test/root-context-names-what-each-list-left
                      seon.print-test/more-says-how-many-and-where
                      seon.print-test/a-one-line-cut-reads-the-source-rest
                      seon.render-test/the-page-says-what-it-keeps
                      seon.render-test/root-context-groups-blocked-tasks-by-what-blocks-them
                      seon.render-test/no-render-calls-clip
                      seon.render-test/a-capped-list-says-how-many-more}}
