 {:seon.task/name "one-owner-per-view-path"
  :seon.task/plan "Session DUP-VIEWS (notes/duplicates-audit-2026-10-22.md, its DUP-VIEWS rows; owner, 2026-10-22: keep src small, resolve every duplicate path at its owner, no guards). Est. -120 src lines. One owner each, the copies deleted: (A1) the declared status sets: web's live?, the server's agents answer and the check harness read seon.root/gone-statuses; one properties reader, seon.contract/properties (seon.render/properties and seon.render.ui/config-panel's own reader delete), and contract/enum-values for the enums' members; seon.problems reads :seon.status/failed (added to :seon.attempt/status in seon.facts.edn) instead of #{:dead :lost}. (A11) root's view numbers (p50s, tx per commit, the windows dropped) are one pure fn, seon.root/view-numbers, which seon.root/state and seon.render.proc/system-value both call. (A12) a test run is red by seon.proofs/red?, read by the card's dots, the card's allowed line, the event's row and the proofs box. (A13) a card's evaluation row is history-row with a compact budget; an item's text is (or :printed :shown), the record keeping :shown for an error too (seon.repl/record-tx), not the error map read as text. (A14) a merge's result in words once (seon.render.ui/merge-words) for the card's pill and the event. (A15) my.root's create!/load-tasks!/load-docs! share one private write-declared!. (A18) the render proc's stats read seon.lib/summ. (A21) the web proc keeps its waiting pages and tabs with seon.step/pend and answered, not its own :next and :waiting. (B2) the second error shape {:error string} goes from the server (every refusal: :seon.root/refused; a defect: the thrown error map or :seon.root/proc-defect), ``seon.mcp/request!`` (an unreachable server; now bin/mcp's JSON-RPC error) and the web listener that cannot bind; the readers' (or (:seon.error/message r) (:error r)) patches in seon.render.proc, seon.render.ui and seon.root/start! delete. (B3) the zoom's {:status :unknown} and web's :bytes-per-s (a key nothing set