 {:seon.task/name "one-printer-and-declared-renders"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-22: \"Do not create more than one value printer and no clipping happens before then. Make custom ai and html renders for all important data agents and humans will want to see\". Worktree session renders (jolt/renders). Audit of src (read 2026-10-22 at c3265a8): 24 display sites made text beside the printer, 14 cuts, 27 literal budgets, 25 wire/storage sites (fine). What each became: (1) the REPL answers every value through `seon.render/printed` (seon.repl/wrap-print): a value whose producer names its schema in its metadata (`seon.task/task`, `seon.problems/report`) reads by its declared :seon.render/ai render, the same text root's context is made from, ending with the form that shows the whole value as data ((with-meta result/h3 nil)); a map that merely holds a key (a partial pull, tx data) prints as data (the review's first finding: dispatching on a key lost data); an eval error's text is its error map's render (wrap-caught), which carries :seon.error/fix (no reader showed it before). (2) `seon.render/schema-of`: an error map's schema is its :seon.error/type (else :seon.error/base), and a producer may name its value's schema in metadata. (3) Declared renders: :seon.error/base ai `seon.render.ai/error` and html `seon.render.ui/error-box` (message, fix, type and operation, problems, the variant's keys), :seon.task/task ai `seon.render.ai/task` (execution, needs, problem, failure, stuck, plan cut with the form that reads the rest, proofs bounded, evidence) and the html task box gaining failure, stuck and evidence, :seon.attempt/attempt ai `seon.render.ai/attempt` (root's context's work lines; it replaces section-work's two line builders), :seon.problems/row ai `seon.render.ai/problem-row` (root's context's and the banner's recorded lines; a :stuck row read the pr-str of producer/owner-ns and a :task-conflict row read attempt nil nil before: now the cause and both sides), :seon.problems/report ai `seon.render.ai/report`. (4) A cost verdict's words are `seon.cost/verdict-lines`, once: the agent's text (`seon.cost/explain`) and the page's box; the page's copy (ui verdict-lines, which lacked the accepted-overrun and regression lines) and the dead seon.render.ai/cost-report go; a cost report's message is not shown twice. (5) Second printers gone: the page serializer `seon.web.html/html` str'd any leaf, `seon.print/line` and `seon.render.ui/prose` str'd a non-string, the config panel pr-str'd each value, a red test's expected/actual (already printed text) were printed again, ai/problems pr-str'd a row, the cut's form in ui/prose, contract.clj's expected schema str'd, db.clj's types-differ message pr-str'd the keys, cost.clj's accepted-overrun line pr-str'd the measure. (6) Cuts: EVENT-CAP, SERIES-CAP and HISTORY-CAP are config keys (:seon.config.render.list/stream, series, history; seon.repl's top-fns is land6's :seon.config.agent/form-top-fns); every literal budget in render.ui, render.ai and render.proc is :seon.config.render/cell-budget, line-budget, part-budget or form-budget; a card shows every warning bounded (it showed the first); value-html's 4000-character threshold goes; the compact card's CSS clip (.dense .ev .printed) goes. (7) The law as a check from the compiler's facts: seon.render-test/one-printer-and-no-cut-before-it imports src and reads :form/refs (seon.program/live-forms); every var printing beside seon.print, and every var of a display namespace that cuts, is named in docs/render.md#one-printer. After land5: an outside model's seon_eval text is its items as the REPL's own text (`seon.render.ai/items`, in `seon.server/mcp-reply`; it was every answer pr-str'd whole as EDN, strings escaped), an error answer by its render, any other answer by the printer; a defect's :data and its JSON-RPC message go through the printer and the error's render; the context's last evaluations show a value whose producer named its render by that render's text, as the REPL answered it (seon.context/shown-evals printed the live value). Shrink rows 22-27 (notes/shrink-research-2026-10-22.md, Brief 5) are folded in. Owed, each its own task: seon.render/the-banner-counts-what-root-counts, seon.render/the-root-tile-counts-the-program-it-loaded, seon.task/an-agent-reads-its-task-as-main-holds-it (the browser check's three), seon.root/root-keeps-what-it-shows-by-config, seon.agent/an-eval-error-carries-its-data, seon.cost/the-page-says-regression, seon.ref/a-summary-says-there-is-more, seon.check/a-check-that-never-hears-back-says-so, and the values without a schema to declare a render on yet: seon.render/a-merge-answer-has-a-schema-and-a-render, seon.render/a-merge-conflict-shows-on-the-page, seon.render/what-a-branch-will-merge-shows-on-the-page, seon.render/a-turn-is-a-row-on-the-agent-page, seon.render/config-shows-where-each-value-came-from, seon.render/spend-has-a-render. The review (2026-10-22) fixed: values stored whole and cut once by their render, budgets read when used, a render's own cut reported, one predicate for a rendered value, each render naming what it leaves, every wire pr-str as seon.edn/encode."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/one-printer-and-no-cut-before-it
                      seon.render-test/an-error-reads-its-message-fix-and-variant
                      seon.render-test/a-task-reads-its-state-plan-proofs-and-failure
                      seon.render-test/an-attempt-reads-in-one-line
                      seon.render-test/every-problem-class-reads-what-it-is-about-and-why
                      seon.render-test/an-outside-model-reads-an-evaluation-as-the-repl-says-it
                      seon.render-test/the-model-reads-a-rendered-value-as-its-repl-did
                      seon.repl-test/an-agent-repl-answers-what-a-clojure-repl-answers
                      seon.repl-test/a-reply-item-carries-values-not-their-printed-text}}
