 {:seon.task/name "a-debug-view-of-any-agent"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-23: \"Lets get the web UI working better so I can get a debug view into any agent.\" Replaces a-turn-is-a-row-on-the-agent-page (its proof included). What exists: /agent/{id} (seon.render.ui/agent-page: zoom-head, zoom-work, proofs-box, the newest context read in zoom-context, the evaluations as history rows), built by seon.render.proc's zoom-value from root's view entry, main's attempt and the agent's branch db. It shows no turn: a turn's facts (:seon.turn/turn-fact: reply, reasoning, calls, tokens, cache hits, split, basis) have no render; it shows only the newest context; an agent root no longer holds (a kept run, another boot) has an empty page; there is no way to message the agent (parity row 73) or release its held task. v1 (~/src/seon/src/seon/render/web.clj debug-response, sent.clj view): /agent/{id}/debug lists each model call (prompt, cached and completion tokens, finish) and opens it into what it was sent, remade from the call's basis (never stored), its sections token-badged; /agent/{id}/message writes a :seon.message fact the next turn's current-state block shows as unread. The page becomes the debug view, every part a render over facts: (1) the head says why the agent is as it is (seon.render.ui/why: its status, its attempt's outcome and reason, its task's held failure, the form it runs), with its attempt, branch, model, pid, memory, fork ms, start, turns, tokens and cost at the model's configured prices (seon.model/cost, the one priced sum; off-peak, said so); (2) a turn timeline, one row per turn in order (seon.render.ui/turn-row, the declared html render of :seon.turn/turn-fact): its tokens, the cache-hit share, cost, time split, finish, its reply and reasoning, each eval call's code and what the REPL answered as the model read it (the turn's :calls, the same text the scrollback sends), the proofs it saw (its basis's results), and the exact context it read, made again by seon.context/render from its basis, with each part's tokens (help page, attempt sections, scrollback, turn sections and each turn key), under the printer's page budget, its cut linking /agent/{id}/turn/{n} where the whole text is served; (3) proofs: the newest turn's set, the judge's (the attempt's results on main) and the agent's last run, each report saying reused or run; (4) the branch: :will-merge as the newest turn measured it, and the attempt's conflicts; (5) the problems main recorded of this agent or its task (seon.problems/report's rows); (6) acting from the page: the eval box (seon.root/submit!, as seon_eval), interrupt (seon.root/interrupt!), a message bar (seon.root/message!: root's existing :message delivery, the request the server's new :message op sends too; the agent's next turn takes its inbox into the block's :messages, recorded in the turn's basis, so the turn's context shows it), and release of a held task (my.root/run!'s one transaction, as a UI call of seon.root/release!); (7) an ended agent's page reads its newest attempt on main and that attempt's branch from the store (branches are kept). Live by events (the branch's t moving), never polled. /ns/{ns} and /data are filed as their own task. Deletes zoom-context's one-read panel (each turn row shows its own) and the attempts table on the page."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/each-turn-is-a-row
                      seon.render-test/a-turn-row-shows-the-context-remade-from-its-basis
